# Paths to your own copy of X-COM Apocalypse (Steam preferred, GOG fallback). Not committed.
APOC_STEAM_FOLDER=%ProgramFiles(x86)%\Steam\steamapps\common\XCom Apocalypse
APOC_GOG_FOLDER=%ProgramFiles%\GOG Galaxy\Games\X-COM Apocalypse
# Tavily web search key for .mcp.json is NOT stored here: set TAVILY_API_KEY as a Windows user
# environment variable (or export it in the shell that launches Claude Code) and restart Claude Code.
#
# API keys for the hosted model arms of `reverseapoc drive` are NOT stored here either. Set each
# one as a Windows user environment variable, then restart the shell or launcher that runs drive.
# The driver reads only the variable NAMES listed in config/driver/backends.toml, never a file.
# Leave unused ones unset; an arm whose key is missing is refused before any session starts.
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  OpenRouter: every hosted arm (DeepSeek V4.1-Flash, GLM-5.3, GLM-4.7-Flash,
#                       Muse Spark Open, hosted Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, the Gemini fallback)
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and ZAI_API_KEY are not used since 2026-11-10 (DeepSeek and GLM run through
# OpenRouter); the driver strips both from every session.
# PowerShell, once per key:
#   [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable('OPENROUTER_API_KEY', '<key>', 'User')
# Codex (GPT arms) and Antigravity (Gemini and GPT-OSS arms) need no key here: they use their own
# sign-in (`codex login`, `agy`). See docs/toolchain.md, "Model API keys and sign-ins".
